 "intro": "Perusia (Perugia), a hill town in Etruria, winter 41-40 BC. Mark Antony’s brother Lucius and his wife Fulvia have raised legions against Octavian. You are Octavian, Caesar’s nineteen-year-old heir, now twenty-two, with Marcus Agrippa.",
 "debrief": "In Appian’s account, Octavian walled Lucius into Perusia while Antony’s generals in Gaul hesitated and failed to break the siege. Lead sling bullets found at Perugia carry crude insults about Fulvia and Octavian. Starved, Lucius surrendered and was spared, but the town was burned. Some later writers claimed Octavian sacrificed 300 men of Perusia on the Ides of March; whether this happened is doubted. The other choices are what-ifs.",
